This module covers how devices find the destination MAC address needed to send data over a local network. I learned how ARP (Address Resolution Protocol) works with IPv4 addresses to find the corresponding MAC address.

Topics Covered
Address Resolution Protocol (ARP)
IPv4 addresses and MAC addresses
How ARP works
ARP requests and replies
MAC address resolution
ARP tables
Communication within a local network

What I Learned
The difference between an IP address and a MAC address.
How ARP maps an IPv4 address to a MAC address.
How a device sends an ARP request to find another device's MAC address.
How the destination device responds with an ARP reply.
How devices store learned IP-to-MAC mappings in an ARP table.
How ARP helps devices communicate within a local network.

